d R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd051-pwd.yaml (full SRD for pwd utility -- read all requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- SIGPIPE handling pattern)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function for SIGPIPE handling)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/pwd/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"pwd utility -- prints current working directory in logical (-L) or physical (-P) mode\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.1 as specified in the SRD -- core default behavior printing the current working directory to stdout with a trailing newline\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.2 as specified in the SRD -- logical mode behavior using PWD environment variable and symbolic link preservation\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.3 as specified in the SRD -- physical mode behavior resolving all symbolic links to the real filesystem path\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.4 as specified in the SRD -- flag parsing, mode selection, and default mode when no flags are provided\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() to match GNU coreutils SIGPIPE behavior -- import github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Build with go build -o bin/pwd ./cmd/pwd/ -- the bin/ directory is gitignored\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Parse flags using the standard library flag package or os.Args manual parsing as dictated by the SRD -- GNU pwd uses long options (--logical, --physical)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/pwd/main.go compiles without errors: go build -o bin/pwd ./cmd/pwd/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/pwd/... reports no issues\"\n   